  "analytic_review": [
    "The complete actual ordinal successor graph, not a repaired lifetime path, independently yields all six endpoint-inclusive5/9 blocks. Every interior physical rank2 fails either complete AABB history or the required next actual R. Complete histories and physical ranks survive all full-drift identifications; different translated blocks therefore cannot overlap, since the later start would have to appear among these events. Equal starts imply the same actual event.",
    "At a given post-LL flat X, the unique cyclic predecessor and its predecessor determine the same V/root unit. Hence distinct quotient roots do not double-charge a block, including full-drift aliases. No long-owner injection is used.",
    "The signed critical first-track theorem places the entire block, including the final L3 departure, inside one actual LEFT-return interval. The block contains R reads, so that interval is not any four-L LL-root return. Critical LEFT intervals are occurrence-disjoint, hence the blocks, four-L roots and actual RIGHT time form disjoint reservations, yielding P>=L_RIGHT+9nP+13nN. This is not an added fuel charge or a bound on P.",
    "Positive D.R0 is off this Gamma: its incoming Y.R2 edge is LEFT, while every Gamma R0 is RIGHT in either geometric role. R.L1 cannot be LEFT-V RIGHT-side because its successor X.R2 is LEFT. The already-signed final supplier report contains this strengthened qualification. Other curves and older stock remain unrestricted."
